<section class="bg-cream py-10 lg:py-12"><div class="container-x">
  <div class="grid gap-8 lg:grid-cols-[1fr_270px]">
    <article class="card prose p-6 sm:p-8">
<h2 class="mod-h2">Educational Philosophy &amp; Convergent–Divergent Thinking</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">UGC NET/JRF Paper-1 — Quick Revision Notes</h3>
<h2 class="mod-h2">1. Educational Philosophy</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">शैक्षिक दर्शन</h3>
<p>Educational Philosophy education के aims, curriculum, teaching methods, teacher–learner role और values को philosophical principles के आधार पर समझाती है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Educational Philosophy = Aim + Curriculum + Method + Teacher–Learner Role + Values</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">A. Idealism — आदर्शवाद</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Main Focus</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Mind + Ideas + Values + Spiritual Development</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Thinkers</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Plato</li><li>Socrates</li><li>Hegel</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Educational Features</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Truth, Beauty and Goodness</li><li>Moral और spiritual development</li><li>Teacher का central और ideal role</li><li>Humanities, literature, ethics</li><li>Discussion और questioning</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Recall</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Idealism → Ideas and Values</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">B. Naturalism — प्रकृतिवाद</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Main Focus</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Nature + Freedom + Child-Centred Education</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Thinkers</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Jean-Jacques Rousseau</li><li>Herbert Spencer</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Educational Features</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Education according to nature</li><li>Learner freedom</li><li>Direct experience</li><li>Minimum external interference</li><li>Teacher as observer/facilitator</li><li>Natural consequences</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Recall</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Naturalism → Nature and Freedom</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">C. Pragmatism — प्रयोजनवाद</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Main Focus</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Experience + Utility + Action + Problem-Solving</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Thinkers</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>John Dewey</li><li>William James</li><li>Charles Peirce</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Educational Features</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Learning by Doing</li><li>Project and problem-solving methods</li><li>Knowledge tested through consequences</li><li>Flexible curriculum</li><li>Democratic classroom</li><li>Teacher as facilitator</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Recall</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Pragmatism → Experience and Action</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">D. Realism — यथार्थवाद</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Main Focus</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Objective Reality + Facts + Scientific Knowledge</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Thinkers</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Aristotle</li><li>Francis Bacon</li><li>John Locke</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Educational Features</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>External world exists independently</li><li>Observation and experiment</li><li>Science and practical subjects</li><li>Inductive method</li><li>Sense experience</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Recall</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Realism → Reality, Facts and Science</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">E. Existentialism — अस्तित्ववाद</h3>
<p class="mod-tag">Main Focus</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Individual Freedom + Choice + Responsibility + Authenticity</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Thinkers</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Søren Kierkegaard</li><li>Jean-Paul Sartre</li><li>Martin Heidegger</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Educational Features</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Learner individuality</li><li>Personal choice</li><li>Self-awareness</li><li>Responsibility for decisions</li><li>Teacher as facilitator of self-discovery</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Recall</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Existentialism → Existence, Choice and Responsibility</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Philosophy Comparison</h3>
<h2 class="mod-h2">2. Convergent Thinking</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">अभिसारी चिंतन</h3>
<p>Convergent thinking में available information और rules का उपयोग करके किसी problem का एक best या correct answer खोजा जाता है।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Convergent Thinking = Many Facts → One Correct Solution</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Characteristics</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Logical</li><li>Focused</li><li>Rule-based</li><li>Accuracy-oriented</li><li>One correct answer</li><li>Standardised testing में उपयोगी</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>25%25\% of 400 कितना है?</p>
<p>एक correct answer: 100</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Association</p>
<p class="mod-strong">J. P. Guilford → Convergent and Divergent Production</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">3. Divergent Thinking</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">अपसारी चिंतन</h3>
<p>Divergent thinking में एक problem या stimulus से अनेक possible ideas, responses और solutions उत्पन्न किए जाते हैं।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Divergent Thinking = One Problem → Many Possible Solutions</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Characteristics</p>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Creative</li><li>Open-ended</li><li>Flexible</li><li>Original</li><li>Multiple answers</li><li>Exploratory</li></ul>
<p class="mod-tag">Example</p>
<p>“एक plastic bottle के अधिकतम alternative uses बताइए।”</p>
<p>इसका कोई एक fixed correct answer नहीं है।</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">4. Components of Divergent Thinking</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Fluency</h3>
<p>अधिक संख्या में ideas उत्पन्न करना।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Flexibility</h3>
<p>Different categories या perspectives से ideas देना।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Originality</h3>
<p>Unique और uncommon ideas देना।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Elaboration</h3>
<p>Idea को detail में develop करना।</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Divergent Thinking = Fluency + Flexibility + Originality + Elaboration</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">5. Convergent vs Divergent Thinking</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Important Principle</h3>
<p>Creative problem-solving में दोनों की आवश्यकता होती है:</p>
<p class="mod-strong">Divergent Thinking generates alternatives; Convergent Thinking selects the best alternative.</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">6. Exam Traps</h2>
<ul class="prose-list"><li>Divergent thinking का अर्थ illogical thinking नहीं है।</li><li>Convergent thinking का अर्थ केवल rote learning नहीं है।</li><li>Creativity में केवल originality नहीं; fluency, flexibility और elaboration भी शामिल हैं।</li><li>Brainstorming मुख्यतः divergent thinking को support करता है।</li><li>Final solution select करना convergent thinking है।</li><li>Guilford को divergent production और Structure of Intellect Model से associate करें।</li><li>Dewey का problem-solving दोनों thinking processes का उपयोग कर सकता है।</li></ul>
<h2 class="mod-h2">7. Quick MCQs</h2>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 1</h3>
<p>A learner produces ten different solutions to reduce classroom waste. This primarily represents:</p>
<p>A. Convergent thinking
B. Divergent thinking
C. Rote learning
D. Conditioning</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer: B. Divergent Thinking</p>
<p>Explanation: एक problem के multiple solutions generate किए गए हैं।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 2</h3>
<p>Selecting the most feasible solution from several alternatives represents:</p>
<p>A. Divergent thinking
B. Convergent thinking
C. Random thinking
D. Imitation</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer: B. Convergent Thinking</p>
<p>Explanation: Alternatives में से best answer select करना convergent process है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 3</h3>
<p>Which educational philosophy is most closely associated with Learning by Doing?</p>
<p>A. Idealism
B. Naturalism
C. Pragmatism
D. Existentialism</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer: C. Pragmatism</p>
<p>Explanation: John Dewey का Pragmatism experience, activity और problem-solving पर आधारित है।</p>
<h3 class="mod-h3">Question 4</h3>
<p>Individual freedom, choice and responsibility are central to:</p>
<p>A. Realism
B. Existentialism
C. Idealism
D. Behaviourism</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Correct Answer: B. Existentialism</p>
<h2 class="mod-h2">Final Recall</h2>
<p class="mod-tag">Idealism → Ideas</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Naturalism → Nature</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Realism → Reality</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Pragmatism → Practical Experience</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Existentialism → Individual Choice</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Convergent → One Best Answer</p>
<p class="mod-tag">Divergent → Many Original Answers</p>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="mod-table"><tr><th>Philosophy</th><th>Main Focus</th><th>Teacher’s Role</th><th>Preferred Method</th></tr><tr><td>Idealism</td><td>Ideas and values</td><td>Role model</td><td>Dialogue and lecture</td></tr><tr><td>Naturalism</td><td>Nature and freedom</td><td>Observer</td><td>Direct experience</td></tr><tr><td>Pragmatism</td><td>Experience and utility</td><td>Facilitator</td><td>Project/problem-solving</td></tr><tr><td>Realism</td><td>Facts and reality</td><td>Subject expert</td><td>Observation/experiment</td></tr><tr><td>Existentialism</td><td>Choice and individuality</td><td>Guide</td><td>Dialogue/self-exploration</td></tr></table></div>
<div class="table-wrap"><table class="mod-table"><tr><th>Basis</th><th>Convergent</th><th>Divergent</th></tr><tr><td>Direction</td><td>Multiple information → one answer</td><td>One stimulus → multiple answers</td></tr><tr><td>Nature</td><td>Closed-ended</td><td>Open-ended</td></tr><tr><td>Focus</td><td>Accuracy</td><td>Creativity</td></tr><tr><td>Answers</td><td>One best/correct</td><td>Many possible</td></tr><tr><td>Process</td><td>Logical selection</td><td>Idea generation</td></tr><tr><td>Assessment</td><td>Objective test</td><td>Project/open-ended task</td></tr><tr><td>Example</td><td>Correct formula select करना</td><td>कई research topics बनाना</td></tr></table></div>
    </article>
    <aside class="lg:sticky lg:top-24 lg:self-start">
      <div class="card p-5">
        <p class="text-[10.5px] font-extrabold uppercase tracking-[0.16em] text-gold-600">Unit 1 · Teaching Aptitude</p>
        <ul class="mt-3 grid gap-1.5 text-[13.5px] font-semibold text-navy-700">
          <li><a href="module-1.html" class="block rounded-lg px-2.5 py-2 hover:bg-navy-50">1. Teaching: Objective, Levels &amp; Basic Concepts</a></li>
